# clang-tidy, run by tools/analysis.py behind tools/analysis-baseline.txt.
#
# The families are on; each check turned off names why (counts: Quoin, 2026-10-16, none of
# them a defect):
#   bugprone-casting-through-void              605: GObject's cast macros, G_OBJECT (x) and
#                                              kin, cast through void *; the advice is C++'s
#                                              reinterpret_cast
#   bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters        62: a style opinion about every (a, b) pair
#   bugprone-reserved-identifier, cert-dcl37-c,
#   cert-dcl51-cpp                              48: names inside GLib's own macros
#                                              (g_str_has_prefix declares __prefix)
#   bugprone-multi-level-implicit-pointer-conversion
#                                               36: g_steal_pointer, g_clear_pointer and kin
#                                              take void **
#   bugprone-assignment-in-if-condition         21: GLib macros (g_str_has_prefix) and the
#                                              while ((x = next ())) idiom
#   bugprone-sizeof-expression                   1: g_set_object's macro
#   cert-err33-c                                 7: fprintf to stderr, which has nowhere to
#                                              report its own failure
#   clang-analyzer-unix.Malloc                   9: the analyzer never runs cleanup
#                                              functions, so every g_autofree on an
#                                              allocation it knows is a "leak"; GCC's
#                                              -fanalyzer, taught GLib's allocators
#                                              (src/analyzer-glib.h), checks g_free instead
#   clang-analyzer-optin.core.EnumCastOutOfRange
#                                               43: GTK's flag enums (0, or several flags
#                                              or'ed together) are not single enumerators
#   clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling
#                                                9: asks for C11 Annex K (memcpy_s), which
#                                              glibc does not have
#   clang-analyzer-valist.Uninitialized          6: Clang 21 does not model C23's
#                                              va_start (__builtin_c23_va_start), so every
#                                              va_arg reads as uninitialized
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  cert-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  -bugprone-casting-through-void,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-reserved-identifier,
  -cert-dcl37-c,
  -cert-dcl51-cpp,
  -bugprone-multi-level-implicit-pointer-conversion,
  -bugprone-assignment-in-if-condition,
  -bugprone-sizeof-expression,
  -cert-err33-c,
  -clang-analyzer-unix.Malloc,
  -clang-analyzer-optin.core.EnumCastOutOfRange,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling,
  -clang-analyzer-valist.Uninitialized
WarningsAsErrors: ''
